From dfc71d515c85063b724794bd041c1382b380a01d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:28:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 086/112] Filters: 7 ms crossfade where a mode or the route
 changes or a filter is switched off

Changing the LPF or HPF mode, the route (H2L / L2H / parallel) or switching a
filter off used to switch at once: the new filter started from a reset or
foreign state, the switched-off one's output vanished, the route jumped
(clicks up to 250x the tone's largest step, +20 to +55 dB above 4 kHz).
Now FilterSet keeps a copy of itself as it was (configuration and state) in
one of 24 shared slots, which renders on beside it for 320 samples (7.3 ms);
the output moves from the copy's to the new one's in a straight line, with
the copy's own gain compensation (on its input for a voice, on its output for
the song / a kit / an audio track). Then the copy goes, and a switched-off
filter with it. A change during a fade waits for its end. Nothing changes
where nothing changes (static hash as before); a filter switched on keeps its
fade-in from the dry signal. All slots busy: switches at once, as before.
A voice frees its slot when it's unassigned; isOn() holds while fading.

tests/filters filter_neutral_test clicks: largest step <= 1.74x (was up to
254x), above 4 kHz at most +3 dB (was up to +55 dB).

